        ['q' => 'What does a public adjuster do?', 'a' => '<p>A public adjuster is licensed by the Texas Department of Insurance to represent the policyholder on a property insurance claim. The work typically includes reviewing the policy, inspecting and documenting the damage, preparing a detailed estimate, presenting the claim to the insurer, and negotiating the amount. The insurance company\'s adjuster works for the insurer; a public adjuster works for you.</p>'],
