    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<p>This page collects the questions we hear most often from homeowners and business owners in Corpus Christi, Nueces County, and the Coastal Bend. The answers explain how Texas law and typical policies work in general. Your own coverage depends on your policy language and the facts of your loss, and nothing here is legal advice. If you want answers about your specific claim, request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a>.</p>

<h2>Public adjusters, fees, and contracts</h2>
<p>A Corpus Christi Public Adjuster represents the policyholder, not the insurer. Texas regulates public adjusters under Insurance Code Chapter 4102, including fee limits, contract terms, and a 72-hour right to cancel. Read more <a href="/about-us/">about us</a> or our longer guide to <a href="/questions-about-public-adjusters/">questions about public adjusters</a>.</p>

<h2>TWIA and windstorm coverage</h2>
<p>Most coastal properties in the Coastal Bend get wind and hail coverage through TWIA, which has its own statutory deadlines for filing, decisions, appraisal, and disputes. Our guide to the <a href="/twia-claim-process-corpus-christi/">TWIA claim process in Corpus Christi</a> covers it step by step.</p>

<h2>Hurricanes, flood, and deductibles</h2>
<p>After a hurricane, many owners are dealing with three policies at once: a homeowners or commercial policy, a TWIA windstorm policy, and a flood policy. Deductibles are often a percentage of the dwelling limit. See <a href="/named-storm-hurricane-deductibles-texas/">named storm and hurricane deductibles in Texas</a> and our <a href="/hurricane-damage-claims-corpus-christi-guide/">Corpus Christi hurricane damage claims guide</a>.</p>

<h2>Claim process and deadlines</h2>
<p>Texas sets response and payment deadlines for most insurers in the Prompt Payment of Claims Act. Our <a href="/claim-deadline-calculator/">claim deadline calculator</a> turns those rules into dates, and <a href="/why-property-insurance-claims-are-delayed-texas/">why property insurance claims are delayed</a> explains common causes of delay.</p>

<h2>Disputes, denials, and documentation</h2>
<p>When the amount is disputed, appraisal may be an option. When coverage is denied, documentation and the policy language matter most. Our free <a href="/claim-tools/">claim tools</a> help you gather weather records, organize your file, and check the numbers.</p>
HTML,
